From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juljus <juljus@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:18:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] fix(daemon): give a client being let go a bounded time to
 take its exit status

Replacing or detaching a client first writes it an exit status, then acks
the control message whose sender waits SHELL_TO_CLIENT_CTL_TIMEOUT for
that ack. A client that stopped reading (a stalled ssh connection)
blocked that write past the wait, and once it failed the shell->client
thread blocked for good handing its ack to nobody: the thread lived but
no attach or detach got through again. That write now gets 100ms.

When the shell exits, the thread now acks first and gives the client up
to 5s for its exit status, so a slow client still gets the shell's real
status while a dead one cannot hold the thread, and the attach joining
it, forever. A client that does not take its status in time is logged at
info.

The shell->client tests share their setup, kill their shell however they
end, and the reset test checks that the heartbeat write really blocked.
